CAT = "hkle1Overview"; SEG = "OVR"
Q = [
("Which body is the main regulator of Hong Kong's securities and futures markets?",
 "The Securities and Futures Commission", ["The Hong Kong Monetary Authority", "Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing", "The Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau"],
 "The SFC is the independent statutory regulator of the securities and futures markets. The HKMA regulates banks, HKEX operates the markets, and the FSTB makes government policy."),
("The SFC was set up in 1989 mainly in response to:",
 "The 1987 market crash review", ["The 1997 handover", "The 2008 global financial crisis", "The launch of Stock Connect"],
 "After the October 1987 crash closed the market for four days, the Securities Review Committee (the Davison Report) recommended a single independent regulator, and the SFC was created in 1989."),
("Which of these is one of the SFC's regulatory objectives under the SFO?",
 "To protect investors", ["To set interest rates", "To guarantee investors' returns", "To manage the Exchange Fund"],
 "Section 4 of the SFO lists objectives including fair, efficient and transparent markets, protection of investors, minimising crime and misconduct, and reducing systemic risk. Interest rates and the Exchange Fund belong to the HKMA."),
("When a bank in Hong Kong deals in securities for clients, its securities business is supervised day to day mainly by:",
 "The HKMA", ["The Insurance Authority", "The MPFA", "The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong"],
 "Banks that carry on regulated activities register with the SFC as registered institutions, and the HKMA acts as their frontline regulator, applying the SFC's standards."),
("The Hong Kong Monetary Authority's main role is to:",
 "Keep money and banks stable", ["License all stockbrokers", "Approve takeover offers", "Run the stock exchange"],
 "The HKMA maintains currency and banking stability, supervises banks and manages the Exchange Fund. Brokers are licensed by the SFC, takeovers fall under the SFC's codes, and HKEX runs the exchange."),
("The Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Authority (MPFA) mainly regulates:",
 "MPF schemes and trustees", ["Listed company takeovers", "Stockbrokers' liquid capital", "Insurance agents' licences"],
 "The MPFA registers MPF schemes and approves and supervises their trustees. Takeovers are an SFC matter, and broker capital is set by the SFC's Financial Resources Rules."),
("Which body oversees the auditors of Hong Kong listed entities?",
 "The Accounting and Financial Reporting Council", ["The Investor Compensation Company Limited", "The Takeovers and Mergers Panel of the SFC", "The Securities and Futures Appeals Tribunal"],
 "The Accounting and Financial Reporting Council (formerly the Financial Reporting Council) regulates the accounting profession and inspects and disciplines auditors of public interest entities."),
("The Investor and Financial Education Council (IFEC) is best described as:",
 "An SFC subsidiary for financial education", ["A tribunal for small investor claims", "An industry trade association", "A fund that repays failed brokers' clients"],
 "The IFEC is a subsidiary of the SFC that promotes financial literacy and education for the public. Compensation for a broker's default comes from the Investor Compensation Fund."),
("A retail client has a monetary dispute with a broker that internal complaint handling has not settled. Which body offers mediation first and arbitration next?",
 "The Financial Dispute Resolution Centre", ["The Market Misconduct Tribunal", "The Process Review Panel for the SFC", "The Joint Financial Intelligence Unit (JFIU)"],
 "The Financial Dispute Resolution Centre runs the Financial Dispute Resolution Scheme on a mediation-first, arbitration-next basis for monetary disputes with financial institutions."),
("Which statement about the Process Review Panel for the SFC is correct?",
 "It checks the SFC's own procedures", ["It hears appeals against SFC fines", "It approves new listing applications", "It sets the SFC's yearly budget"],
 "The Process Review Panel is an independent panel that reviews whether the SFC follows its internal procedures fairly and consistently. Appeals against SFC decisions go to the Securities and Futures Appeals Tribunal."),
("Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing Limited (HKEX) is treated under the SFO as:",
 "An exchange controller", ["A government department", "A registered institution", "A wholly owned SFC subsidiary"],
 "HKEX is a listed company that controls the Stock Exchange, the Futures Exchange and the clearing houses, and it is recognized by the SFC as an exchange controller."),
("Which HKEX subsidiary clears and settles trades in shares listed on the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong?",
 "HKSCC", ["HKCC", "SEOCH", "OTC Clear"],
 "Hong Kong Securities Clearing Company (HKSCC) runs CCASS for shares. HKCC clears futures, SEOCH clears stock options, and OTC Clear clears OTC derivatives."),
("Within the HKEX group, which company clears stock options traded on the Stock Exchange?",
 "SEOCH", ["HKSCC", "HKCC", "The SEHK itself"],
 "The SEHK Options Clearing House (SEOCH) clears and settles stock options. HKCC clears futures and options traded on the Futures Exchange."),
("What is the main difference between the SFC and HKEX?",
 "The SFC regulates; HKEX operates", ["HKEX licenses all brokers' staff", "The SFC owns the stock exchange", "Each prosecutes the other's cases"],
 "HKEX operates the exchanges and clearing houses as a commercial listed company, while the SFC is the statutory regulator that supervises HKEX and licenses intermediaries."),
("Which government body is responsible for financial services policy and for proposing new securities laws to the Legislative Council?",
 "The Financial Services and the Treasury Bureau", ["The Takeovers and Mergers Panel", "The Securities and Futures Appeals Tribunal", "The Hong Kong Monetary Authority's board"],
 "The FSTB sets financial services policy within the Government and takes legislation through the Legislative Council. The SFC advises and implements."),
("Who appoints the members of the SFC's board?",
 "The Chief Executive", ["HKEX's board", "The Legislative Council by vote", "The Chief Justice"],
 "The SFC's chairman, chief executive officer and other directors are appointed by the Chief Executive under the SFO, with a majority of non-executive directors."),
("A person who places money in a fund through a licensed corporation is, in market terms, best described as:",
 "An investor", ["A principal of the corporation", "An intermediary", "A support service provider"],
 "Investors supply capital; intermediaries such as brokers and fund managers stand between investors and the market; support service providers include share registrars and custodians."),
("Which firm is a market intermediary rather than a support service provider?",
 "A licensed securities broker", ["A listed company's share registrar", "A trustee for a unit trust", "A firm's external auditor"],
 "Brokers, dealers, advisers and asset managers are intermediaries licensed or registered for regulated activities. Registrars, trustees and auditors support the market without dealing for clients."),
("The SFC's Intermediaries Division is mainly responsible for:",
 "Licensing and supervising firms", ["Approving every IPO prospectus alone", "Prosecuting market misconduct cases", "Running the clearing houses"],
 "The Intermediaries Division handles licensing and the supervision of licensed corporations. Enforcement handles investigations and prosecutions; HKEX runs the clearing houses."),
("Which SFC division vets takeover and merger transactions under the Takeovers Code?",
 "Corporate Finance", ["Enforcement", "Investment Products", "Supervision of Markets"],
 "The Corporate Finance Division administers the Takeovers Code and Share Buy-backs Code and oversees listing matters, with the Takeovers Executive acting within it."),
]
